    "campaign_summary": "Peruvian digital security authorities report six critical threats: WatchGuard Agent and Gitea suffer critical remote code execution vulnerabilities affecting versions prior to 1.25.13.0000 and 1.17–1.27.0 respectively; Keycloak has account-takeover vulnerability CVE-2026-18963; APT Kimsuky conducted spear-phishing campaigns using OneDrive malicious links delivering .LNK files targeting South Korea and Japan with data extraction and credential harvesting capabilities; new trojans E4del and PINHOLE exploit FTP server banners for malware delivery on Windows; Comfast CF-N1-S router has critical buffer overflow vulnerability CVE-2026-77148. Immediate patching and defensive measures are recommended across all affected systems and organizations.",
